WEBVTT

00:02:18.729 --> 00:02:23.919
Young Godai, would you
see that Kyoko gets this?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.830
I think she should be the one
to keep it, not me.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.920
It's Soichiro's diay.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.140
Why do I have to be the one
to deliver this?

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.080
If I return the diay,

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.010
the manager will start
to miss her husband again.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.180
I'm not giving it to her.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.530
Welcome back!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.560
You're still up?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.740
Just tidying up the shoes.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:41.870
Could these be Mr. Yotsuya's?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.380
You were out quite
late tonight.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.230
I uh...was at the pinball parlor
near the station.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:54.730
Here.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.670
Please call when you're
going to be late.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.600
I have to lock up.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.110
I uh...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.150
Good night!

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:40.280
What's the matter, Godai?
You look so glum.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.720
Stop sighing like
the world's got you down.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:52.310
You'll make us depressed too.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.820
You call that "depressed"?!

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.420
You're partying in my room
and you say YOU'RE depressed?

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:07.500
Blame your drinks, not us.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.210
Young Godai, you did something
to the manager, didn't you?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.520
I-I didn't do anything.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:21.960
You're up to something.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.250
No, I'm not!

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.650
You can't keep secrets from us.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.090
Gimme a break.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:35.120
How could I?
I can't do anything for her.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:40.040
You're right...
You're too chicken.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.420
No guts...

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:42.840
Loser.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.270
Now see here!

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.210
Party time!

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:02.150
Too chicken, no guts...
Can't find a bride!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.900
It's a lovely day...
Perfect for laundry.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.220
Aren't you going to do
your wash, Mrs. Ichinose?

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.880
I'll do everything
tomorrow.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.650
What a wonderful breeze!

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:03.490
Coming!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:09.710
Yes?

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.960
Good morning, Godai.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:16.720
I was...

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:21.700
supposed to give
this to you yesterday.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:26.510
From my father-in-law?

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.050
What could it be?

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.550
Come with me!

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.140
What the heck are
you doing?!

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.940
What did you to
to the manager?

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.470
Huh? Nothing...

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.280
You'd keep secrets from me?

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.680
Why're you looking
at me like that?

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.520
I haven't done anything
to be ashamed of.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.170
Then what's going on?

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.890
I gave her the diary Mr. Otonashi
asked me to give her, that's all.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.070
A diary?!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.400
I had no idea Soichiro
kept a diary.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.470
This is just around
the time we met...

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.680
Did he write about me?

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.710
When did Soichiro begin
to have feelings for me?

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.420
July 8:

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:55.740
"There may never be a day
like today again."

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.830
After a breakfast of
mackerel in miso sauce...

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.560
the school principal treated me
to a lunch of miso mackerel.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:10.440
When I got home, there was
leftover miso mackerel.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:13.790
Three meals of miso mackerel...

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.850
Coincidence or no, it was
a vey strange day.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.550
What is this?!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.240
July 9: Grilled fish, grated radish,
miso soup with mushrooms.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.870
July 12: Tempura.
The shrimps were tiny.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.150
July 15: Grilled salmon,
boiled spinach.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:46.940
July 16: Curry rice.
Medium-spicy tastes best.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:50.970
July 18: Mixed rice with
vegetables. Test today.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.290
Is this really his diary?

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:03.630
There's nothing about me,
or even about school.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.550
"I received this postcard
from her. I'm puzzled."

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:16.410
Who could it be?

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.050
What postcard?

00:12:28.900 --> 00:12:31.300
"I've been thinking about
her since yesterday,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:32.820
but I don't know
what to do."

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:35.770
"Should I reply?"

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:40.300
"This has never happened
to me before."

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:46.440
He's so confused. He didn't
even mention his meals.

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:50.050
Whom could it have been from?

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:54.080
August 2:
I'm still at a loss...

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.810
Concentrating only on my studies,
I've never even looked at women.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.680
Receiving a postcard
like this

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:03.760
puts me in a dilemma.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.030
I can't even swallow my food.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:11.030
I never sent Soichiro
such a suggestive postcard.

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:17.140
Maybe Soichiro had...

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:19.960
...someone else!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.320
When he wrote this
Soichiro was 27...

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.350
It'd be odd if he DIDN'T
have a steady girlfriend.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:34.120
What could've happened
to the postcard?

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.470
Maybe it's at his father's.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.240
11:00 p.m...?

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:56.950
I shouldn't call this late.
It wouldn't be right.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:03.180
Anyway, it's all in the past.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.070
I'll hang up if he doesn't
answer after five rings.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:38.950
Hello. Otonashi speaking.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.240
Hello?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:45.740
Hi, Kyoko! You got the
diary? I'm glad.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.200
I thought the time was right
to return it to you.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.720
You should be able to read it
without getting sentimental.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:56.590
Did you read it, Father?

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:01.540
I gave up along the way.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:03.830
What about the postcard?

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:04.950
Postcard?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.100
There was a postcard.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.500
What about the postcard?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:12.650
Never mind. I'm sorry
for calling so late.

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:15.570
Goodnight.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.070
Maybe the postcard got mixed up
with Godai's things...

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.200
What's the matter?

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:43.780
You don't look happy.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:47.420
Not at all -- I'm fine.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.210
Just fine.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.150
I'm off.

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.440
For your daily nap?

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:03.230
To study!

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:08.870
The diay made her recall her
husband, after all...

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.540
Godai?

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:14.370
Yes?

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:18.150
Don't worry about it.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:25.420
I'm not worried at all --
Did it show on my face?

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.900
Was it that obvious?

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:33.330
It doesn't bother me, really!
See ya!

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:35.700
I was talking about
the postcard!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:53.190
Yo, Godai!

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:56.540
You so broke, you can't
buy lunch?

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:01.250
It isn't anything so
material, Sakamoto.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.040
What is it, then?

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:05.330
Let's say, for example, that...

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:10.110
the husband of the woman you love
more than anyone passes away.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.520
Then her husband's diary
shows up.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:19.340
The diary describes every detail
of their happy lives together.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.540
How would you feel if
you read it?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.030
I see...

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:31.710
The manager's husband's
diary turned up, right?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:33.310
And so?

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.700
That's the last time
I tell you anything!

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.180
Just right.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:14.260
I guess I'll just
have to ask.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:39.710
Young Godai isn't home yet.

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:46.450
M-Mr. Yotsuya!
What're you doing here?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.400
Watching the place.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:57.260
This is...!

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:17.890
It was in your bag?

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:20.360
I'm sorry.  I didn't
realize it was there.

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.170
This is the postcard I sent.

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:39.640
Receiving a postcard
like this...

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.700
puts me in a dilemma.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.800
I never sent such
a suggestive postcard.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.430
Did you...read it?

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.950
I uh... Yes.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:00.160
Postcards are hard not to.

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:03.440
I'm sorry...

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.370
Not that I meant to
you understand!

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:09.110
I just saw it...
Sorry.

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:17.300
Thank you!
Thank you so much...

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:18.940
So very much!

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:48.410
'Bye!

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:53.300
Have a good day!
Study hard!

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.990
What did you do to
the manager?

00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:11.370
Returned the postcard,
that's all.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:18.100
Soichiro noticed me
from way back then.

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:25.710
He was all worked up over
such an innocent postcard.

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:45.050
Summer Greetings.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:52.620
Godai's grandmother pays him
a surprise visit.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:57.800
The three of us visit
Mr. Mitaka's home.

00:23:58.280 --> 00:24:02.680
Next: "Overpowered By Love!
Grandma Yukari's Gold-Tooth Challenge!"

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:05.590
I didn't know Yukari
was her name.
